      "id": "01-origins",
      "side": "left",
      "era": "1500 BCE\u2013900 CE",
      "location": "Mesoamerica",
      "title": "Ancient Origins",
      "caption": "Olmec and Maya peoples cultivated cacao in Mesoamerica. For the Maya, cacao was a sacred gift from the gods. Used in rituals and ceremonies, cacao drinks became symbols of life, power and connection, long before chocolate took the familiar form of bars and confections.",
